# Text is stored and checked out with LF on every platform, whatever core.autocrlf says (Git for Windows sets it to
# true). Several checks compare files byte for byte: the conformance vectors must re-dump to themselves
# (unity/core-tests JsonTests.EveryVectorFileRoundTrips), the web page copies must match their sources, and the
# release archives ship what is checked out. Unity rewrites the YAML it touches with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Visual Studio's solution files are committed with CRLF: kept byte for byte, never converted.
*.sln -text
